<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Multiplying vectors by scalars</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\mathbf{a} = {@col(av)@}\) and \(\mathbf{b} = {@col(bv)@}\).</p><p>(a) Find \({@kk@}\mathbf{a}\).</p><div>\({@kk@}\mathbf{a} =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find \([[if test="is(q<0)"]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} - {@abs(q)@}\mathbf{b}[[else]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} + {@q@}\mathbf{b}[[/if]]\).</p><div>\([[if test="is(q<0)"]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} - {@abs(q)@}\mathbf{b}[[else]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} + {@q@}\mathbf{b}[[/if]] =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A scalar multiplies every component; it never adds to them.</p><p>(a) Multiply each component by \({@kk@}\): \({@kk@}\mathbf{a} = {@kk@}{@col(av)@} = {@ta@}\). [[if test="is(kk<0)"]]The scalar is negative, so the vector is reversed: both signs change.[[else]]The scalar is positive, so the direction stays the same.[[/if]]</p><p>(b) \({@p@}\mathbf{a} = {@col(p*av)@}\) and \({@q@}\mathbf{b} = {@col(q*bv)@}\). Add matching components: \([[if test="is(q<0)"]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} - {@abs(q)@}\mathbf{b}[[else]]{@p@}\mathbf{a} + {@q@}\mathbf{b}[[/if]] = {@tb@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
col(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]]);
/* Design: multiples and combinations of column vectors. a is drawn from AL, which leaves out the chapter's example and exercise vectors. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Section B, B2 and B3(a). */
AL: [[-5,-4],[-5,-3],[-5,-2],[-5,-1],[-5,1],[-5,3],[-5,4],[-4,-5],[-4,-3],[-4,-2],[-4,-1],[-4,1],[-4,2],[-4,3],[-4,5],[-3,-5],[-3,-4],[-3,-2],[-3,-1],[-3,1],[-3,2],[-3,4],[-3,5],[-2,-5],[-2,-4],[-2,-3],[-2,-1],[-2,3],[-2,5],[-1,-5],[-1,-4],[-1,-3],[-1,-2],[-1,2],[-1,3],[-1,4],[-1,5],[1,-5],[1,-4],[1,-3],[1,-2],[1,3],[1,5],[2,-5],[2,-4],[2,-1],[2,1],[2,4],[2,5],[3,-4],[3,-1],[3,2],[3,4],[4,-5],[4,-2],[4,1],[4,3],[4,5],[5,-4],[5,-2],[5,-1],[5,4]];
av: rand(AL); a1: av[1]; a2: av[2];
b1: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]); b2: rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[0]); bv: [b1,b2];
kk: rand([-3,-2,2,3,4]); p: rand([2,3]); q: rand([-3,-2,2,3]);
ta: col(kk*av); tadd: col(av+kk); ttop: col([kk*a1,a2]); tabs: col(abs(kk)*av);
tb: col(p*av+q*bv); tnob: col(p*av+signum(q)*bv); tsgn: col(p*av-q*bv);
tw1: ta+matrix([1],[0]); tw2: tb+matrix([1],[0]);
badm: matrix([x],[1]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
